    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">How to Use These Guides</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 mb-3">
        <li><strong>Pick one guide that matches your symptoms.</strong> Start with the two or three points it highlights rather than trying every point at once.</li>
        <li><strong>Locate each point carefully.</strong> Use the anatomical reference points given and confirm the spot by tenderness and a slight depression.</li>
        <li><strong>Apply steady pressure.</strong> Press at a 90-degree angle and hold for about 30 seconds to 3 minutes while breathing deeply.</li>
        <li><strong>Use acupressure alongside, not instead of, your usual care.</strong> Stop and see a healthcare provider if symptoms persist, worsen, or concern you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">If you are pregnant or managing a chronic condition, review the safety section before using any of these protocols.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 cursor-pointer">Can I treat several conditions at once?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">Yes, but it is usually better to focus on the two or three most relevant points per session. A 10-20 minute session covering 4-6 points is plenty.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 cursor-pointer">How long before I notice a change?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">For acute symptoms like a tension headache or nausea, relief can come within minutes. Chronic conditions typically respond to consistent daily practice over one to two weeks.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 cursor-pointer">Are these protocols safe for everyone?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">They are written for generally healthy adults. If you are pregnant, have a chronic condition, or take medication, read the safety section first and check with your healthcare provider.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 cursor-pointer">What if a protocol does not work for me?</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">Results vary from person to person. Try a different point from the guide, adjust your pressure and hold time, or see your doctor if symptoms persist, worsen, or concern you.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
